    "title": "Bill to make Hillsborough superintendent an elected role clears Senate - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Divya Kumar ,\n7 hours ago Rep. Michael Owen, R-Apollo Beach, shown here in 2024 in Tampa, sponsored the bill to let voters decide if Hillsborough County Schools superintendent should become an elected position. [ PHOTO BY DIRK SHADD/TAMPA BAY TIMES ] The bill that would put making the Hillsborough County schools superintendent an elected position on the ballot this November cleared its last obstacle in the state legislature, moving through the Florida Senate.\nThe move came the day after the Hillsborough County school board voted to extend existing superintendent Van Ayres’ contract until January 2029 and expressed concerns about what the new rule could mean.",
